💭 A closure written in a specialization has the specialized type as 👇, so the methods it calls on 👇 are
💭 specialized too, also in nested closures, and return values of the concrete type the closure returns.
🕊 🔲🐚T ⚪️🍆 🍇
  🖍🆕 value T
  🆕 🍼 value T 🍇🍉
  ❗️ 🔓 ➡️ T 🍇
    ↩️ value
  🍉
  ❗️ 🔐 ➡️ T 🍇
    🍇 ➡️ T
      ↩️ 🔓👇❗️
    🍉 ➡️ get
    ↩️ ⁉️get❗️
  🍉
  ❗️ 🪆 ➡️ T 🍇
    🍇 ➡️ T
      🍇 ➡️ T
        ↩️ 🔓👇❗️
      🍉 ➡️ inner
      ↩️ ⁉️inner❗️
    🍉 ➡️ outer
    ↩️ ⁉️outer❗️
  🍉
  🖍❗️ 🔄 new T 🍇
    new ➡️ 🖍value
  🍉
  💭 A closure in a mutating method calls a mutating method on 👇.
  🖍❗️ 🎛 new T 🍇
    🍇
      🔄👇 new❗️
    🍉 ➡️ set
    ⁉️set❗️
  🍉
🍉

💭 An escaping closure captures an instance of a class.
🐇 🫙🐚T ⚪️🍆 🍇
  🖍🆕 value T
  🆕 🍼 value T 🍇🍉
  🔏❗️ 🔓 ➡️ T 🍇
    ↩️ value
  🍉
  🔏❗️ 🔐 ➡️ 🍇➡️T🍉 🍇
    ↩️ 🍇🎍🥡 ➡️ T
      ↩️ 🔓👇❗️
    🍉
  🍉
🍉

